# One collapsed action for all three skills, rather than separate
# PandaPick/PandaPlace/PandaPush actions.
#
# Why collapsed: the planner emits a single `chosen_skill` enum
# (vlm_task_planner.py:73-79, RobotSkill = PUSH|PICK|PLACE) inside one
# NextBestAction object, and bridge_node.py dispatches all three down a
# shared path. Three separate actions would mean three clients, three
# servers and a dispatch switch on both sides to carry what is already
# one field.
#
# Field names mirror NextBestAction exactly (vlm_task_planner.py:88-128)
# so the executor is a straight field copy with no renaming. The ROS 1
# executor renamed them and got it wrong twice - it read `action.skill`
# (AttributeError, the field is `chosen_skill`) and `target_location`
# (silently empty, the field is `placement_object`). Keeping the names
# identical is what stops that recurring.

# --- Goal ---
string chosen_skill                     # "pick" | "place" | "push"
string target_object                    # object to pick, place, or push
string placement_object                 # "" unless chosen_skill == "place"
string push_direction                   # "" unless chosen_skill == "push"; "left" | "right"
bool should_grasp_at_specific_section   # false unless chosen_skill == "pick"
bool should_place_at_specific_section   # false unless chosen_skill == "place"
---
# --- Result ---
bool success
string message                          # failure reason, or a short note on success
---
# --- Feedback ---
string status                           # human-readable progress, e.g. "moving to standoff"
